org_raw:
Housing and Family Services of Greater New York, Inc. - Housing
Preservation - Council District 40 Kensington, PLG, Ditmas Park;
Crown Heights, Flatbush

purpose_raw:
Communities for Healthy Food integrates food access & community development;
expanding access/awareness of affordable/healthy food via outreach, education,
training, food sector jobs, & new/improved food outlets.

Funds will be used to provide activities and special events for seniors in the community;
including exercise classes, parties / entertainment, and outings to cultural events
throughout NYC.

Funds will be used to support CLT-related tenant and community organizing;
community education, outreach and legal and technical support for CBOs and
emerging CLTs in Council District 41.

To provide funding support for: benefits & entitlements assistance; legal services;
housing counseling & advocacy; Immigration Assistance; ESOL & HSE (GED) programs;
Computer Classes; Financial, Employment & Senior Services; and After School
Programming.

To provide funding support for education reform, equity, green/open spaces;
retrofitting for energy efficiency; and mapping arts resources. Funds will support
staffing, space rental, training materials, and facilitation of community events.

Funding will be used for community organizing, and counseling activities, address
issues including direct housing needs such as eviction prevention and housing security;
environment and public health needs; education including job and leadership training.

Support for legal services and organizing programs as follows: 1) Legal representation;
2) Advocacy; 3) Tenant Organizing; and 4) Community Organizers educate and mobilize
residents around impact issues facing the community.

Funds will support programming at Schools: CCBQ @ PS 50 Queens; High School for
Construction Trades, Engineering, & Architecture; PS 161 Arthur Ashe School;
Richmond Hill High School.

Funding will be used to sustain a vegetarian and halal soup kitchen for the homeless in
Manhattan; defray costs for the Toys for Tots toy drive; supplies and equipment;
delivery of goods; promotion & marketing of events; & staffing for program activities.

Advising and/or processing applications for property tax abatements, foreclosure
intervention, resiliency, healthy homes initiatives, home maintenance training;
guidance & referral on how to resolve municipal liens.

Funding to support BronxConnect Court-Involved Youth Mental Health Initiative;
providing youth involved in the justice system with psychosocial assessments,
internships, referrals for services, leadership development and anger management.

Funding to support community engagement discussions, roundtables, and workshops;
and to underwrite ticketing costs allowing the organization to provide fully subsidized
tickets.
